WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.704
Lukas: The old leader disappears. Would you promote immediately?

2
00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:08.976
Raj: No. A fencing token needs storage-side enforcement.

3
00:00:08.976 --> 00:00:13.225
Raj: Just to confirm, stale writers get rejected, right?

4
00:00:13.225 --> 00:00:16.945
Hannah: Where is the new epoch persisted and checked?

5
00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:21.025
Raj: The quorum decision persists it in replicated storage.

6
00:00:21.025 --> 00:00:24.721
Lukas: What if that rejection mechanism can't be verified?

7
00:00:24.721 --> 00:00:29.665
Raj: Pause writes. Use verified power fencing if needed.

8
00:00:29.665 --> 00:00:34.106
Raj: The out-of-band console can independently confirm shutdown.

9
00:00:34.106 --> 00:00:39.218
Hannah: Okay, maybe define a rollback trigger for uncertainty.

10
00:00:39.218 --> 00:00:44.930
Raj: Stop routing writes. A smoke test follows safe authority transfer.

